 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our claims-triage agent (ADK, running on Agent Engine in europe-west3, Gemini 2.5 Pro behind it, Firestore for session state) is supposed to go live for the German insurer client on Nov 14. Their DPO just sent over a list: DPIA input, record of processing activities, a data flow diagram showing where stuff goes incl. any calls out to Vertex in other regions, and a 'system description' for their works council. I've got the README, the terraform, and our design doc in /docs. Can you figure out which regs actually apply here (GDPR obviously, but does the EU AI Act kick in for insurance claims?) and draft these? Mark anything you're guessing about so I can send it to their legal people."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Need help with the compliance pack for the benefits eligibility assistant we built for a UK council + a pilot with a Canadian province. They want an algorithmic impact assessment, the UK ATRS transparency record, a CAIQ-style vendor security questionnaire filled in, and something on cross-border transfers since logs land in us-central1 right now. Go off the repo + the ARCHITECTURE.md + our data_inventory.yaml. Don't invent controls we don't have, just flag gaps for counsel."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "security team flagged that our ADK agent logs full user messages incl. emails and phone numbers to Cloud Logging. can you add a redaction step before the logging callback fires? code is in agent/callbacks.py, we use before_model_callback already", "needs_instead": "A code change: implementing PII redaction in the agent's logging/callback pipeline, not drafting legal or compliance documents."}
]}
